[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles Unified Calibration and Service Interface Software Requirements Specification
UID: DHF-HRC-UCSI-0001
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-ucsi

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the software requirements for the Heracles Unified Calibration and Service Interface (UCSI).
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
UCSI is a technician-facing service interface for the Heracles superficial radiation therapy system. It is available as a standalone application and as a module hosted by the system PC software. It presents system telemetry, status, and servicing information and provides manual high-voltage power supply (HVPS) control for service activities, including manually initiated X-ray emission.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
===================  ==========================================
Abbreviation/Term    Definition
===================  ==========================================
HVPS                 High Voltage Power Supply
SDS                  Software Design Specification
SRS                  Software Requirements Specification
UCSI                 Unified Calibration and Service Interface
===================  ==========================================
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: RQ-UCSI-
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-001
TYPE: Interface
TITLE: Deployment modes
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall provide the UCSI service interface when operated as a standalone application and when hosted by the system PC software.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-002
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: System telemetry and status
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to view current system operating parameters, communication status, system status, interlock status, and active faults.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-003
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Telemetry monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to select system operating parameters for numerical monitoring and graphical display of their telemetry history.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-004
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Manual HVPS service control
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to command HVPS operating parameters and to enable and disable manual X-ray emission for service activities. The software shall display the associated HVPS feedback and interlock status to the operator.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-005
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Coil service control
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to command coil operating parameters for service activities and to view the associated coil feedback values.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-006
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Control system configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to view and set control system configuration values for service activities.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
